# JobPrep Works — Open Edition
#
# Copy to .env and edit. Every value is optional except the provider settings
# in section 1 — the defaults shown are what you get if you leave a line out.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing here leaves your machine except the calls you configure below: the
# LLM provider you pick, and (optionally) a web-search API for company research.


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 1. Your model provider — pick ONE block and uncomment it
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# This is the only section you have to touch. LLM_API_KEY works for every
# provider. The conventional per-vendor name is accepted too, but ONLY the one
# belonging to the provider you picked: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for anthropic,
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY for openrouter, OPENAI_API_KEY for openai and for the
# OpenAI-wire servers (openai-compat, llamacpp, vllm). So a key already
# exported in your shell just works, and an unrelated one lying around in your
# shell is never sent to a provider it does not belong to.
#
# Note that a variable exported in your shell WINS over the same name in this
# file — python-dotenv does not override the environment. `unset` it if this
# file is meant to be the source of truth.

# ── Anthropic Claude (default) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only provider with a built-in model default, so a key alone is enough.
# Get a key: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# ── OpenAI ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL defaults to https://api.openai.com/v1.
# Get a key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#LLM_PROVIDER=openai
#OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#LLM_MODEL=gpt-5

# ── OpenRouter (hundreds of models behind one key) ───────────────────────────
# Base URL defaults to https://openrouter.ai/api/v1. Model ids are
# provider-prefixed — see https://openrouter.ai/models for exact slugs.
#LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
#OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
#LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5
# Route only to model hosts that may not retain or train on prompts. Your
# career documents ride in these prompts, so this is ON by default; turning it
# off widens the pool of eligible hosts (and can be cheaper).
#OPENROUTER_NO_TRAINING=1
# Optional attribution shown on openrouter.ai dashboards:
#OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE=JobPrep Works
#OPENROUTER_HTTP_REFERER=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ── Ollama (fully local, nothing leaves your machine) ────────────────────────
# Uses Ollama's native API, which is the only way to set a real context window
# and get server-enforced structured output. Install: https://ollama.com
# Then: ollama pull qwen3:14b
# Pick a model with solid instruction-following and JSON output; very small
# models (under ~7B) will struggle with the extraction schemas.
#LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
#LLM_MODEL=qwen3:14b
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# Ollama's own default context is 4096, which silently truncates long résumés
# and postings. Raise it as far as your hardware allows.
#LLM_NUM_CTX=16384

# ── Any other OpenAI-compatible server (llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio, …) ───────
# No default base URL — you must set one.
#LLM_PROVIDER=openai-compat
#LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
#LLM_MODEL=your-model
#LLM_API_KEY=                  # most local servers ignore this
# Without LLM_API_KEY these three fall back to OPENAI_API_KEY, since that is
# the name their own clients read. Set LLM_API_KEY explicitly (even to a dummy
# value) if you do not want a real OpenAI key sent to your LLM_BASE_URL.

# ── Canned responses, no model at all (UI work, demos, offline) ──────────────
# Every pipeline returns fixed sample data instantly. Nothing is called.
#LLM_PROVIDER=mock

# Per-call timeout in seconds. Local models on modest hardware are slow —
# raise this rather than shrinking LLM_NUM_CTX.
#LLM_TIMEOUT_S=180


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 2. Company Pulse — employer research with web search
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The Pulse tab researches an employer: ratings, recurring complaints, recent
# news, with sources. It needs a way to reach the web, and how depends on your
# provider:
#
#   Anthropic / OpenAI / OpenRouter  the model searches server-side. Works out
#                                    of the box; nothing to configure.
#   Ollama / llama.cpp / vLLM        the model cannot search, so THIS APP runs
#                                    the searches and hands over the results.
#                                    Set one of the API keys below.
#
# With no search available the Pulse tab hides itself; everything else works.

# auto (default) = native where the provider supports it, otherwise whichever
# API key below is set. Force a specific one with tavily | brave | searxng.
# Set to 'off' to disable company research entirely.
#WEB_SEARCH=auto

# ── Option A: Tavily — built for LLM use, easiest setup, free tier ───────────
# https://tavily.com  →  API key
#TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...

# ── Option B: Brave Search — independent index, free tier ────────────────────
# https://brave.com/search/api/
#BRAVE_API_KEY=BSA...

# ── Option C: SearXNG — self-hosted, nothing shared with a search vendor ─────
# Any instance with the JSON format enabled. To run your own:
#   docker run -d -p 8888:8080 -e SEARXNG_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32) searxng/searxng
# then add "json" to search.formats in its settings.yml.
#SEARXNG_URL=http://localhost:8888

# Turn company research off completely (hides the Pulse tab).
#RESEARCH_ENABLED=1
# Use a different provider/model for research than for everything else.
# Research is long-context judgment work — point this at your most capable
# option if your main model is small. Unset = same as LLM_PROVIDER/LLM_MODEL.
#RESEARCH_PROVIDER=auto
#RESEARCH_MODEL=
# Searches per research run, and full pages fetched (native search only).
#RESEARCH_MAX_SEARCHES=6
#RESEARCH_MAX_FETCHES=2
# Hard per-run spend ceiling in USD. Only enforceable where the provider
# reports cost (OpenRouter does); local models are free and report nothing.
#RESEARCH_COST_BUDGET=1.50
#RESEARCH_TIMEOUT_S=300
# Research lookups allowed per UTC day. Opening a company you've already
# researched is free; only new research and refreshes count. There is no
# refresh cooldown — you can re-research an employer whenever you want, so this
# is the only bound. 0 = unlimited.
#PULSE_DAILY_LIMIT=25
# Seconds between sweeps that resume research interrupted by a restart
# (0 disables the sweeper).
#PULSE_POLL_INTERVAL=60
# Server-tool identifiers, only if a provider renames one before this app
# catches up. Leave unset unless research fails with an unknown-tool error.
#ANTHROPIC_WEB_SEARCH_TOOL=
#ANTHROPIC_WEB_FETCH_TOOL=
#OPENAI_WEB_SEARCH_TOOL=


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 3. Spend guard (optional)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Nothing in this app is gated behind a plan — every feature is always
# available. This is purely a brake against a runaway loop or a mis-click on a
# batch action quietly draining a paid API key while you're not watching.
#
# Units per UTC day; roughly one unit per action you take. 0 = no limit
# (the default). Today's count is shown on the Settings page either way.
#LLM_DAILY_LIMIT=0
# Ledger rows older than this are collapsed into a per-day summary and pruned.
#LLM_LEDGER_RETENTION_DAYS=90
#LLM_LEDGER_SWEEP_INTERVAL=86400


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 4. Storage
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Everything lives here: the SQLite database and your uploaded documents.
# Back it up by copying the directory. Deleting it is a full factory reset.
#JOBPREP_DATA_DIR=./data
# Database filename (absolute paths also work).
#JOBPREP_DB=jobprep.db
# Seconds a write waits for the database lock before failing. Raise it only if
# you see "database is locked" with several pipelines running at once.
#DB_BUSY_TIMEOUT=15


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 5. Limits and behavior (rarely changed)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Largest file you can upload, in bytes (default 10 MB).
#MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=10485760
# Character caps before text reaches a prompt. Postings and documents get the
# large one; interview answers get the small one, so a pathologically long
# answer can't multiply the cost of every grading call.
#MAX_TEXT_CHARS=200000
#MAX_ANSWER_CHARS=8000
# Background pipelines are in-process, so stopping the server mid-run would
# strand a job "in progress" forever. Every REAPER_INTERVAL seconds, anything
# stuck longer than REAPER_STALE_MINUTES is marked failed-and-retryable. Raise
# the stale window if you run a slow local model (it must exceed your longest
# legitimate run). 0 disables the sweeper.
#REAPER_INTERVAL=300
#REAPER_STALE_MINUTES=30
# Threads available to background pipelines and page loads together.
#THREADPOOL_TOKENS=100


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 6. Exposing this beyond localhost (usually: don't)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# There is no login. Anyone who can reach the port has full access to your
# documents and can spend your API credits. Keep it bound to 127.0.0.1 unless
# you have put real authentication in front of it.
#
# If you do expose it, pin the Host header (a comma-separated allowlist)
# against DNS-rebinding attacks from pages you visit:
#TRUSTED_HOSTS=*
# Interactive API docs at /docs and /redoc (off by default).
#ENABLE_DOCS=0
